      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For subtlety, focus on behavioral inconsistencies rather than just appearance. Watch for guests who exhibit extreme nervousness or overly aggressive patterns when interacting with staff, or those who seem to be using the hotel as a temporary base for extended, secretive meetings. Other subtle flags might include an unusually high number of simultaneous, discreet phone calls, or difficulty providing basic details despite appearing sophisticated. Training your staff to observe these patterns helps maintain the desired exclusive ambiance without causing offense.",
